infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title From promise to proof: making a fetch type true
  desc Each rung makes the annotation less of a lie; only the top one inspects the bytes
  order asc
  sequences
    - label as User — cast
      desc Asserts a shape, runs zero checks. A pure promise about the wire; a renamed field or a null sails straight through.
    - label Discriminated union / Result
      desc Forces every caller to handle the failure branch. Honest control flow, but the payload is still cast — unchecked.
    - label OpenAPI codegen / shared type
      desc Type is mechanically tied to the contract: drift closed. Bytes still unverified — a server that breaks its own spec slips by.
    - label zod .parse at runtime
      desc Inspects the real bytes and narrows on success. Trust gap closed — the promise finally becomes a proof.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #0ea5e9 #10b981
